Fixed Template to solve mirror/symmetrical type of pattern questions
====================================================================

Same Tree
=========

code: class Solution {
    boolean fun(TreeNode p , TreeNode q)
    {
        if(p==null && q==null) return true;
        if(p==null || q==null) return false;
        if(p.val!=q.val) return false;
        boolean left = fun(p.left,q.left);
        boolean right = fun(p.right,q.right);
        if(left==true && right==true) return true;
        else return false; 
    }
    public boolean isSameTree(TreeNode p, TreeNode q) {
        return fun(p,q);
    }
}

Symmetric Tree
==============

code: class Solution {
    boolean fnc(TreeNode p, TreeNode q)
    {
        if(p==null && q==null) return true;
        if(p==null || q==null) return false;
        if(p.val!=q.val) return false;
        boolean first = fnc(p.left,q.right);
        boolean second = fnc(p.right,q.left);
        if(first==true && second==true) return true;
        else return false;

    }
    public boolean isSymmetric(TreeNode root) {
        if(root==null) return true;
        return fnc(root.left,root.right);
    }
}

Invert Binary Tree
==================

code: class Solution {
    void fun(TreeNode root)
    {
        if(root==null) return;
        TreeNode temp = root.left;
        root.left = root.right;
        root.right = temp;
        fun(root.left);
        fun(root.right);
        return;
    }
    public TreeNode invertTree(TreeNode root) {
        fun(root);
        return root;
    }
}

Lowest Common Ancestor
======================

code: class Solution {
    TreeNode ans = null;
    int fun(TreeNode node, TreeNode p, TreeNode q)
    {
        if(node==null) return 0;
        int left = fun(node.left,p,q);
        int right = fun(node.right,p,q);
        int self = 0;
        if(node==p || node==q) self = 1;
        int total = left+self+right;
        if(total == 2 && ans == null) ans = node;
        return total; 
    }
    public TreeNode lowestCommonAncestor(TreeNode root, TreeNode p, TreeNode q) {
        fun(root,p,q);
        return ans;
    }
}

Binary Search Tree : Parent node ki value kuch bhi hosakti hai , parent ke left wala jo node hoga woh parent se less hoga aur jo parent node ke right wali value hogi woh parent se jada hogi.
==================

Why BST? because BST sorted hota hai aur searching mein time complexity kam lagti hai , same as binary Search

Search in a Binary Search Tree
==============================

code: class Solution {
    TreeNode ans = null;
    void fun(TreeNode root , int val)
    {
        if(root==null) return;
        if(root.val==val)
        {
            ans=root;
            return;
        }
        else if(val<root.val) fun(root.left,val);
        else fun(root.right,val);
    }
    public TreeNode searchBST(TreeNode root, int val) {
        fun(root,val);
        return ans;
    }
}

T.C.: O(Logn) , yaha pe hum har node nhi dekh rahe hai , har ek level pe ek node dekh rahe hai, that is no. of levels, kisi bhi binary tree mein no. of levels hota hai logn. Same like binary Search, yaha pe bhi har baar half subtree eliminate hojata hai either left or right.

